== 2026-11-20 12:45:53 #1025 route (c): the power of a dd sign reading at k_c 55, D 17.5, and the dd horizon series' accuracy there. Written before the run.
Why: dd_b12_cause_note.log. A ~1e-10 error in block 12 alone moves ln|det| by 0.1-2.5, and the float64 one flips the sign, while noise at
1e-14 on all of M and 1e-15 on blocks 0-11 does not. A dd sign reading is only tested if the check can see an error of that size.
(1) Check A2 at D 17.5 (ell_ddm.py sshres, lam 1.93, u 0.01 and 0.005, the D 13 bar 1e-24; u 0.04 for information): PASS if the worst
residual is <= 1e-24. Control: --mutate=lam must FAIL.
(2) dd_b12_noise.py (venv-1025dd): the hybrid M (float64 blocks 0-11, dd block 12) at lam 1.92, 1.935, 1.9505, 1.955; relative noise
eps * xi on block 12's entries only (added in double-double), eps 1e-20, 1e-16, 1e-14, 1e-12, 1e-11, 1e-10, 1e-9, 4 seeds; dd_logdet.
Power condition (the control, must hold): the sign flips for >= 1 (lambda, seed) at some eps <= 1e-9. If it never flips, the sign is not
sensitive to block 12 at the double size, which would contradict the cause note, and the reading stops.
Pass: no flip, and |shift of ln|det|| <= 1e-4, at eps <= 1e-16 at every lambda and seed.
Report: eps*, the smallest eps with a flip, and the margin eps* / (A2's worst residual) as a rough measure of how far the dd horizon block
is from flipping the sign (the residual is not the block's error, so this margin is an estimate, not a bound).
